    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "in Pℓ(D). We introduce the space of piecewise-polynomial functions Pℓ(Th) := {v ∈ L2(Th) : v|K ∈ Pℓ(K), ∀K ∈ Th} with respect to the partition Th and the space of piecewise-polynomial functions Pℓ(Fh) := {vˆ ∈ L2(Fh) : vˆ|F ∈ Pℓ(F), ∀F ∈ Fh}"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 9,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 62.362, 610.288, 532.92, 660.784 ],
    "font" : "LMRoman10-Regular",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "with respect to the skeleton Fh of the mesh Th. The subspace of L2(Th,Rm×n) with components in Pℓ(Th) is denoted Pℓ(Th,Rm×n). Likewise, Pℓ(Fh,Rm×n) stands for the subspace of L2(Fh,Rm×n) with components in Pℓ(Fh). We finally consider"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 10,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 128.72, 583.912, 466.556, 607.855 ],
    "font" : "LMMathItalic10-Regular",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Pℓ(∂Th,Rm×n) := ϕ ∈ L2(∂Th,E); ϕ|∂K ∈ Pℓ(∂K,Rm×n), ∀K ∈ Th ,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 11,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 62.362, 556.943, 287.651, 579.711 ],
    "font" : "LMRoman10-Regular",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "where Pℓ(∂K,Rm×n) := F∈F(K) Pℓ(F,Rm×n)."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 12,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 62.362, 506.042, 532.914, 556.539 ],
    "font" : "LMRoman10-Italic",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Remark 2. It is important to keep in mind that, by definition, the functions in L2(∂Th,Rm×n) and Pℓ(∂Th,Rm×n), are multi-valued on every interior face F, whereas the functions in L2(Fh,Rm×n) and Pℓ(Fh,Rm×n) are single-valued on each face F."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 13,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 62.362, 429.33, 532.918, 506.295 ],
    "font" : "LMRoman10-Regular",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We consider n ∈ P0(∂Th,Rd), where n|∂K = nK is the unit normal vector of ∂K oriented toward the exterior of K. Obviously, if F = K ∩ K′ is an interior edge/face of Fh, then nK = −nK′ on F. If φ ∈ Hs(Th,Rm×n), with s > 1/2, the function φ|∂Th ∈ L2(∂Th,Rm×n) is meaningful by virtue of the trace theorem. For the same reason, if φ ∈ H1(Ω,Rm×n) then φˆ := φ|Fh is well defined in L2(Fh,Rm×n)."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 14,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 79.298, 415.781, 461.549, 438.549 ],
    "font" : "LMRoman10-Regular",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "For k ≥ 0, we introduce the finite-dimensional subspaces of H1 and H2 given by"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 15,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 62.362, 374.074, 446.187, 415.216 ],
    "font" : "LMRoman10-Regular",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "H1,h := Pk+1(Th,Rd×2) and H2,h := Pk(Th,Rdsym×d) × Pk(Th), respectively."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 16,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 79.298, 360.525, 321.952, 375.984 ],
